    {
      "paragraphId": "P00046",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[46]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 4253,
      "endIndex": 4501,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "1. Air Them Out: Natural fibers bounce back beautifully. If your cotton or linen shirt gets a bit rumpled or sweaty, just hang it up in the bathroom while you take a hot shower. The steam will naturally release the wrinkles and freshen the fabric.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00047",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[47]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 4501,
      "endIndex": 4698,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "2. Roll, Don't Fold: When packing your suitcase, tightly roll your T-shirts and joggers instead of folding them. It saves a ton of space and actually prevents hard, permanent creases from forming.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00048",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[48]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 4698,
      "endIndex": 4855,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "3. Wash Cold When You Can: When you finally get to a laundry machine, stick to cold water. Hot water in hotel laundromats can easily shrink natural fabrics.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
